==English==
{{wikispecies|Eugenia}}

===Etymology===
{{ety|en|:af|stop<id:cease moving>|-er<id:agent noun>|text=+|tree=1}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈstɒp.ə/|a=RP}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈstɔp.ə/|a=AusE}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈstɑ.pɚ/|a=GenAm}}
* {{audio|en|En-au-stopper.ogg|a=AU}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɒpə(ɹ)|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Someone or something that [[stop]]s something.
#* {{quote-book
|en
|year=1960
|author=w:P. G. Wodehouse
|title=w:Jeeves in the Offing
|section=chapter IX
|passage=“It just shows you what women are like. A frightful sex, Bertie. There ought to be a law. I hope to live to see the day when women are no longer allowed.” “That would rather put a '''stopper''' on keeping the human race going, wouldn't it?” “Well, who wants to keep the human race going?”}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2000|author=Carole B. Cox|title=Empowering Grandparents Raising Grandchildren|page=28
|passage=Often, in our conversations we encourage people to talk, or we manage to stop them. This can happen without our even thinking about it. Following is a list of conversation starters and '''stoppers'''.}}
# A type of [[knot]] at the end of a rope, to prevent it from [[unravel]]ling.
#: {{ux|en|Put a '''stopper''' in the knot.}}
# A [[bung]] or [[cork]].
#: {{ux|en|We need a '''stopper''' or the boat will sink.}}
# {{lb|en|informal|soccer}} [[goalkeeper|Goalkeeper]].
#: {{ux|en|He's the number one '''stopper''' in the country.}}
#* {{quote-web|en
|date=January 15, 2011
|author=Saj Chowdhury
|title=Man City 4 - 3 Wolves
|work=BBC
|url=http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/eng_prem/9357962.stm
|page=
|passage=And just before the interval, Kolarov, who was having one of his better games in a City shirt, fizzed in a cracker from 30 yards which the Wolves '''stopper''' unconvincingly pushed behind for a corner.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260823160054/http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/eng_prem/9357962.stm|archivedate=23 August 2026}}
# {{lb|en|finance|slang}} In the [[commodity]] [[futures market]], someone who is long (owns) a futures contract and is demanding delivery because they want to take possession of the deliverable commodity.
#: {{ux|en|Cattle futures: spillover momentum plus evidence of a strong '''stopper''' (i.e., 96 loads demanded) should kick the opening higher.}}
# {{lb|en|rail transport}} A [[train]] that calls at all or almost all [[station]]s between its [[origin]] and [[destination]], including very small ones.
# {{lb|en|botany}} Any of several [[tree]]s of the [[genus]] ''[[Eugenia]]'', found in [[Florida]] and the [[West Indies]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1890|author=Charles Sprague Sargent|title=The Silva of North America: A Description of the Trees which Grow Naturally in North America Exclusive of Mexico
|passage=Red Stopper. Leaves ovate-oblong, contracted at the apex into long points, coriaceous. ''Eugenia Garber''}}
# {{lb|en|nautical}} A short [[rope]] for making something [[fast]].
# A [[playspot]] where water flows back on itself, creating a [[retentive]] feature.

